WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.810
So, last week we posted some photos on our
Facebook page showing a pile of rubbish that

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.120
was dumped near the Kaiapoi River.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.300
Most of you were pretty upset about it, and
rightly so, it's disgusting and we all have

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.500
to pay to clean it up.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.640
So we've recreated a trailer load of rubbish

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.940
similar to what was found near the Kaiapoi River.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:24.680
We've got stuff in here like a baby car seat,
a mattress, a kitchen benchtop, an oven,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.780
a sneaker, some polystyrene and just some other
bits and pieces similar to what was found.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:33.130
So we're going to take this trailer load of
rubbish through the Southbrook Resource Recovery Park

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.410
and show just how inexpensive it is to
deal with rubbish properly.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.680
So we're at our first stop in the recycling
area and we're going to get rid of the oven.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.750
Items like ovens can be dropped off for free
at the scrap metal and whiteware section.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.960
Cardboard and polystyrene can also be recycled
for free.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.900
Also shown in the photos was a baby car seat.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.540
You can now bring these to the Resale Store
and recycle them for just $5.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.619
It's much cheaper than taking it into Christchurch
to recycle and it doesn't matter what condition

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:09.090
it is in or even if it's expired, it's still
just $5.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.009
If the mattress and benchtop were in good
condition, these could also be dropped off

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:15.280
to the Resale Store.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.760
And so we'll take the rest of the stuff through
to the refuse area.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.160
So, total cost: $36, really easy

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.580
and most of the stuff we brought along was
able to be recycled.

